description:
Curated by Richard Chappell Dance, the evening brings three works into CULTVR.


&nbsp;

&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
As part of CULTVR’s Catalyst 360, Chappell combines his production Land Empathy with Heart Land, his 2022 BBC Arts dance film. Live dance, intergenerational performers and 360° film projection surround audiences with immersive images of bodies and landscapes, moving from ecological grief towards compassion and renewal.


&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
TIMEWASTERS, by dancer Faye Tan and artist, costume designer and maker George H. Wale, takes a playful turn. Tan wrestles with, clambers over and is engulfed by Wale’s inflatable sculptures and costumes, exploring outdoor leisure and personal narrative.



Who Do You Think I Am? by Neus Gil Cortes combines acro-dance and augmented reality, inviting audiences to share their responses to migration, identity and belonging. In a climate of polarised debate, it creates space for conversation, empathy and different perspectives.
&nbsp;
Date: 11th September 2026
Doors Open: 6.30pm
Performance Starts: 7.30pm
Q&amp;A starts: 8.30pm
Performance Ends: 9.30pm

CULTVR Turns 7!
Join us as we celebrate CULTVR&#8217;s 7th Birthday as the UK&#8217;s first permanent immersive arts centre. Mark the occasion with an evening of DJs, immersive visuals and great company as we celebrate with our community. To say thank you for your support over the years, tickets are just £7.
Featuring:
Rito Digital with support from Movement81 + Lose Yourself to Dance
Experience an immersive electronic music journey from Chile to Swansea and Cardiff as Rito Digital, Movement81 and Lose Yourself to Dance transform the space into a living landscape of sound, generative visuals and collective energy.
Blurring the boundaries between performance and ritual, Rito Digital creates contemporary ceremonies where sound, light and digital environments converge to evoke connection, presence and inner exploration. Drawing from immersive design, XR technologies, and audiovisual art, each performance transforms space into a responsive ecosystem, inviting audiences to move beyond passive viewing into embodied participation.
Movement81 will set the tone with an immersive live AV performance blending uplifting electronics, minimal techno and evolving visuals. Lose Yourself To Dance will start the night, transitioning beats from the garden into the dome.
Join us for an invitation to step into a shared digital ritual shaped by energy, interaction and collective flow.
&nbsp;

&nbsp;
Alma Digital Studio is a multidisciplinary new media art studio founded in Santiago, Chile by multimedia artist Vicente Manzano. They merge art, science, and spirituality to create immersive, interactive environments. By utilising bio-feedback tech and neurotechnology, they craft experiences that promote well-being and inner exploration Their work explores human perception and inner exploration through mediums like interactive VR installations, generative audiovisuals, and mixed-media experiences.
&nbsp;

Movement81 is the electronic moniker of duo Jason&amp;Becky, exploring the interconnected wormholes between 80s indie synth and 90s dance in a spaceship from the future, powered by the collective energy of today. Piloted by two Swansea-based Fine Artists and philosophical researchers, Jason&amp;Becky, their flightpath often connects with the wider themes of their art practice, realised through immersive, interactive audio-visual (AV) installations. Their electronic music &amp; live AV performances meander between uplifting dance &amp; pensive minimal techno, blending resampled audio &amp; visuals with new &amp; original material.
&nbsp;

&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Lose Yourself to Dance is a fresh house and disco night where live musicians and vocalists perform alongside DJs, bringing your favourite tunes to life.
&nbsp;
